# Public frontend content

Apply this policy to public frontend changes and their maintenance scripts.

- Write product text and frontend source comments in English; no literal Hangul.
- Use a modern, uncluttered design with Lucide icons, consistent spacing and
  typography, responsive layouts, and accessible light/dark theme styling.
  Prefer local SVGs, visible keyboard focus, and reduced-motion support.
- Escaped non-English input aliases and language-support test inputs may remain.
- Do not publish internal system/deployment/model information, developer
  diagnostics, personal data, credentials, or visitor profiles.
- Retain public agent connection facts and official service contacts only when
  useful to the user. Preserve security and privacy controls.
- Update Home and all applicable page/social/agent metadata with feature changes.
- Chat presents one relevant agent ranked by recent successful verification,
  recent activity, then quality grade, with newest replies first and connection/verification
  information. Never show free/paid, payment, billing, pricing, fees, cost,
  plan promotions, provider amounts, or wallet details in Chat or its detail view.
- Honor explicit A2A/MCP/x402 selection or a single protocol in the question;
  rank within that protocol. Default unspecified new requests to A2A; retain
  protocol context for details/alternatives. Explicit Any searches all three.
  Keep protocol preference separate from delivery.
- Align global English-first UX with factual footer policies. Link optional task
  updates to admin Visiting Agents without inferring marketing permission.
- Browser notifications require native permission, a native PushSubscription, and
  confirmation by clicking the delivered test notification. Manual polling is
  explicitly separate. Declining pending verification deletes the request.
- Record optional marketing permission separately, unchecked by default, and expose
  eligibility only after destination verification. Support independent withdrawal
  and admin inspection/filtering; advertising delivery remains disabled.
- Run secure-coding and isolated dynamic API/browser security checks after work.
- The user operates the server in their terminal; do not stop/restart it or run
  a competing server without an explicit request. Use isolated test apps/data.
- Keep tokens in session transport and hide raw response JSON, visitor identity,
  and developer examples from the Chat interface.
- Preserve truthful machine API fields; presentation restrictions must not
  misrepresent provider capabilities or alter the selection priority.
- Keep embedded HTML and extracted_html.txt synchronized and run frontend
  content, browser, and security checks after changes.
